\f2\b0 \cf0 All right, I was born July 29, 1993 at 4:29 PM at Evanston Hospital. I was born with a condition called plagiocelphaly diagnosed with at nine months of age and had a surgery for when I was nine months old my earliest memories are living with my mom and my dad and Rogers Park, my mom and dad had taken custody of a friend of my dad's daughter while he was in prison. Her name was vanity, and she was only a year or two older than me. I was around four years old the very first specific memory I have I think is my fourth birthday party and it's me being upset at my party about something and coming out into the party after being told that there's a crown and there was in fact the clown who was my mother's friend Shannon my mom and dad didn't have a great relationship. My dad was nine years older than my mom and I was conceived when my mom was 17 so yeah, my dad was almost 30 and my mom was barely legal. she turned 18 in 1993 and I was born July 29 that year. Both of them came from really hectic, family backgrounds, but from what I understand my mom really was trying her best to mother me and vanity at some point. My mom says that my dad returned vanity or gave her up to the state or something. All I know is that vanity was gone and my dad got rid of her and he did so without consulting anybody and it's something that my mother will never forgive my dad for and I guess now that I think about it, neither will I another odd memory I have looking at that house is finding a homeless person living under the front porch it was rare that I lived in a house in my lifetime, but we rented a large house in Rogers Park and my mom had a garden in the backyard and she grew corn and it was really big house but I found this homeless person and I told him my family and they called the police and moved him. This day homelessness plagues the neighborhood and it is just getting worse. Anyway, sometime after that, my parents divorced and I remember asking my dad why he can't just apologize to my mom and I remember them living in separate apartments and going back-and-forth. My mom is a bartender and my dad worked in IT so when my dad would bring me in the morning to my mother's house before he had to go to work. My mom would be usually sleeping for the first hour or so after I got there and then this time I remember getting in shenanigans such as being hungry and making myself mayonnaise and butter sandwiches after my mom discovered that it was rare that she was sleeping while I was there lol. Another memory from this time was being just exhausted at my dad's house in the morning and in the bathroom supposed to be changing into my clothes for the day to be brought to my mother's house, but I guess I was just too exhausted so I laid down on the floor and went to sleep my dad opened the door and screamed. Oh my God oh my God I guess he thought I was dead, but I was confused and I woke up and I was like huh? What lol . My memories of kindergarten are mainly positive but before it ended, my dad ONe a stuffed wolf at a carnival for me i named koko this was my safety security blankey and first favorite ankmalAnyway, right around the time right before kindergarten my dad would also take me to this caf\'e9 down the block called Caf\'e9 ENNUI or he would have espresso and he would teach me how to read or like force me to figure out how which I did easily and I was reading before kindergarten so when I entered kindergarten, I did really really well and I have two random specific memories from that time. First memory I have is I was in line with my class in the hallway and the boy in front of me had a cool lunchbox and I wanted to see the picture of it, but he refused\'85 Actually, he may have been behind me in line because I elbowed him right in the gut. I was told straight away that that was not the right thing to do. I don't really remember the exact consequence for it though lol the second specific memory I have is my mom bringing me to school one day and she must've been in a rush so all she said I love you this and that she didn't actually give me a hug and I was very forlorn about this the whole day to the point where the whole class noticed and my teacher conducted a class hug everyone in the class gave me a big hug and I love that very much. Then I guess I think the summer before first grade I had my second surgery for. The condition that I spoke about this one was supposedly just to make sure that everything was keeping in line with my growth and these surgeries were done at Rush Hospital. Actually, I have another memory from kindergarten and it was picture day. I grew up with very buck teeth and an overbite and I remember smiling for picture day in the whole class busting out loud laughing and I also remember kindergarten graduation because I had a very love dress that my mom got from me aunt Carson Perie Scott. First grade and second grade get kind of confusing because this is where my mom I guess started turning more into hard drugs and things to start up coming very unstable, but I have a very specific memory of telling a classmate in first grade that I was gonna grow up to be a bad girl. They shouldn't hang out with me because I was gonna grow up to hang out with boys and smoke cigarettes lol actually I have a lot of memories now flooding in from this time but I just wanna move on with the basics, by second grade. It was obvious that I had ADHD because apparently I couldn't keep my desk together, and I wouldn't turn in my assignments, but all of them would be completed just crammed into my desk by the end of second grade. My dad had moved to an entirely different neighborhood of Chicago I think at the time I think now it's considered Bucktown my address is 1735 W. Erie, but because of this, he also took custody of me even though it wasn't like legal custody of me but he was taking full-time care of me because my mom had to walk him into a full-blown heroin addiction but my dad's alcoholism really wasn't much better but third grade is when I was entered into Catholic school. I wasn't baptized anything specifically but that year I chose to become Catholic and I took all the classes and on the Easter vigil I got confirmed baptized in my first communion.\
